{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792605336,"nonce":"Y30xPGOYVcbzLwiNSpXX6krwcuA=","title":"Index structural typedef fields for hover and completion","message":"Anonymous type expressions keep their field types, but the field-access symbols made during lowering can retain an invalid type. Hover uses the symbol rather than the expression type, so valid structural field reads lose their hint. Structural typedef field declarations also had no indexed symbols or source documentation entries.\n\nRecord the inferred type on an unresolved field-access symbol after field inference. Create editor source identities for structural typedef fields, including optional and nested fields, using the actual typed target and source spans. Index their source comments and find their owning alias for cross-file hover and completion documentation. Follow alias chains without guessing by field name.\n\nProtocol coverage opens a consumer before its imported typedef file, checks typed field reads and documented completions through an alias, then opens the defining file and checks normal, optional and nested field declarations.","files":null}]}